                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f1c96798-1915-3a83-ad60-2e540ae7a8ff",
                        "entry_id": "95712eea-4904-313e-9b62-8c11f33cb120",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. связанный, соотносящийся по значению с существительным диахрония, связанный с рассмотрением исторического развития тех или иных явлений"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e14bb6bd-2824-4b54-9acc-dedc099b9eb8",
                                "sense_id": "f1c96798-1915-3a83-ad60-2e540ae7a8ff",
                                "text": "Нам кажется, что наш диахронический анализ подтверждает результаты синхронического."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "577379d6-ef9f-4947-8644-4f694df5f402",
                        "source_entry_id": "95712eea-4904-313e-9b62-8c11f33cb120",
                        "source_sense_id": "f1c96798-1915-3a83-ad60-2e540ae7a8ff",
                        "target_lang_word": "diachronic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diachronic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78b51a8c-0bcd-35a9-812e-ae3e160417ed",
                                        "entry_id": "1b421445-a079-3da4-8435-966865af0029",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Occurring over or changing with time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5573b4d4-93f1-41d2-9a47-99b52bef2255",
                                                "sense_id": "78b51a8c-0bcd-35a9-812e-ae3e160417ed",
                                                "text": "[…] one salient value of archival magazine preservation is that individual issues register, however unintentionally, the small, incremental, diachronic movements within a culture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c7f8d75-26c1-3d30-bacd-b02f450a0c1f",
                                        "entry_id": "1b421445-a079-3da4-8435-966865af0029",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, pertaining to or concerned with changes that occur over time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "418da6e3-0735-4b84-ae46-c08afbe6597f",
                                                "sense_id": "1c7f8d75-26c1-3d30-bacd-b02f450a0c1f",
                                                "text": "It is plain that natural science has developed more diachronic concern, more of the longer historical approach in its interests and repertory, in the last two centuries than in the two millennia before."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "440a03b1-578e-4312-b79f-e66673ee9edb",
                                                "sense_id": "1c7f8d75-26c1-3d30-bacd-b02f450a0c1f",
                                                "text": "I also take a more diachronic perspective and relate the growth of empire to changes in the regional market system as they occurred in the transition from the Early Aztec to the Late Aztec periods."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34646f6a-da72-4429-b1d8-269eff9c5159",
                                                "sense_id": "1c7f8d75-26c1-3d30-bacd-b02f450a0c1f",
                                                "text": "In short, it's usual for the syuzhet to appear more diachronic at the beginning and more synchronic at the end."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a0fae91-9ff9-409a-a7cb-809de471fa1b",
                                                "sense_id": "1c7f8d75-26c1-3d30-bacd-b02f450a0c1f",
                                                "text": "Rethinking the revolution issue is therefore the key to any novel interpretation, but it needs to be addressed in a more diachronic and synchronic fashion, comparing the Wende to earlier German upheavals and to the concurrent transformation of East Central Europe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f2d29a0-093c-4641-a35b-c355077deb86",
                                                "sense_id": "1c7f8d75-26c1-3d30-bacd-b02f450a0c1f",
                                                "text": "2012, Paolo Ramat, Sturtevant's paradox revisited, Thomas Stolz, Hitomi Otsuka, Aina Urdze, Johan van der Auwera (editors), Irregularity in Morphology (and Beyond), [page 61],\nConsequently, the perspective will be more diachronic than synchronic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "631be6b3-503e-4ed9-a6bb-251c920d104a",
                                                "sense_id": "1c7f8d75-26c1-3d30-bacd-b02f450a0c1f",
                                                "text": "However, his interpretation and conclusion receive their rationale almost as often from the subjective horizon as the more diachronic oriented commentaries do."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0a69146f-0288-4f15-bb9a-4fb2e06d3208",
                        "source_entry_id": "95712eea-4904-313e-9b62-8c11f33cb120",
                        "source_sense_id": "f1c96798-1915-3a83-ad60-2e540ae7a8ff",
                        "target_lang_word": "diacronico",
                        "target_lang_code": "it",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diacronico",
                                "target_lang_code": "it",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2af03a38-d3e1-3f04-8e99-e7f10595a7f0",
                                        "entry_id": "7ec76ba1-d845-3235-90bf-df8b026f9932",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "che è relativo alla diacronia"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "63c24765-4542-43ce-9b0f-22eca8159b5e",
                        "source_entry_id": "95712eea-4904-313e-9b62-8c11f33cb120",
                        "source_sense_id": "f1c96798-1915-3a83-ad60-2e540ae7a8ff",
                        "target_lang_word": "diachronisch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diachronisch",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43f04717-e86b-396d-8fc2-940871d59a22",
                                        "entry_id": "02dc768b-3cc8-3b7a-b70a-5accabe66d05",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "die Sprachgeschichte (Diachronie) betreffend"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfd2674c-19e8-45c0-b4db-6e7fa580a42d",
                                                "sense_id": "43f04717-e86b-396d-8fc2-940871d59a22",
                                                "text": "„Außer in der graphischen Gestalt ihrer Elemente unterscheiden sich die beiden Systeme: diachronisch durch ihre Entstehung und synchronisch durch die Funktionen, die sie in schriftlichen Texten haben.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74020acf-6b60-43df-a465-5f4ec922013f",
                                                "sense_id": "43f04717-e86b-396d-8fc2-940871d59a22",
                                                "text": "„Auch die dynamisch-geschichtliche Sprachentwicklung, die diachronische Achse, ist zu berücksichtigen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22d8843e-bb3a-4e48-a65a-12a03b050034",
                                                "sense_id": "43f04717-e86b-396d-8fc2-940871d59a22",
                                                "text": "„Onomasiologie und Semasiologie untersuchen die lexikalischen Einheiten und Beziehungen sowohl unter synchronischem als auch unter diachronischem Aspekt, also sowohl den Zustand als auch die Veränderungen des Systems der Benennungen und der Wortbedeutungen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5cb2959-a238-3e50-a73a-5bba54553e28",
                                        "entry_id": "02dc768b-3cc8-3b7a-b70a-5accabe66d05",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "geschichtlich, historisch dokumentiert"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "general"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e522fe8-ff57-4a49-8061-76f68a30a0c7",
                                                "sense_id": "d5cb2959-a238-3e50-a73a-5bba54553e28",
                                                "text": "„Wenn man Entwicklung als existentielle Metapher im Sinne eines Nicht-Mehr-Zurückkönnens (diachronisch) auffaßt, so ist dem Movement im gewandelten Verstehen von Participatory Democracy eben solches widerfahren.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "42fce3d4-59ed-4a8b-9f33-f653d52ac2be",
                        "source_entry_id": "95712eea-4904-313e-9b62-8c11f33cb120",
                        "source_sense_id": "f1c96798-1915-3a83-ad60-2e540ae7a8ff",
                        "target_lang_word": "art zamanlı",
                        "target_lang_code": "tr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "art zamanlı",
                                "target_lang_code": "tr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6a2ed22-0174-3c3f-bfc6-ded50cd433af",
                                        "entry_id": "e0ba3774-bd74-3139-b559-8b64bb98c46d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Evrim açısından ele alınan süre içinde birbirini izleyen, diyakronik"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a7aa3426-6778-4c42-a26f-747c6fc2c269",
                        "source_entry_id": "95712eea-4904-313e-9b62-8c11f33cb120",
                        "source_sense_id": "f1c96798-1915-3a83-ad60-2e540ae7a8ff",
                        "target_lang_word": "diachronique",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diachronique",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f7554ed-7a9a-3028-b9e8-e452b14d4fee",
                                        "entry_id": "8921aa5f-f996-3cd7-994c-d59d9583dd38",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est relatif à la diachronie, à l’évolution d’un fait dans le temps."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe27690a-557a-4b84-997f-b763208cc74e",
                                                "sense_id": "8f7554ed-7a9a-3028-b9e8-e452b14d4fee",
                                                "text": "Du point de vue diachronique, il faudrait analyser la vie des parémies retenues depuis le Moyen Âge jusqu'à nos jours, afin de découvrir l'évolution morphosyntaxique des parémies et de déterminer leur utilisation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46d7d3f8-f1a7-4f38-8591-66d7f2579329",
                                                "sense_id": "8f7554ed-7a9a-3028-b9e8-e452b14d4fee",
                                                "text": "L'origine onomatopéique d'un lexème est une question diachronique, sans pertinence en tant que telle pour la sémantique de la parole : ainsi, il n'est pas fondamental pour nous de trancher parmi les nombreux cas qui peuvent faire débats (quid de gong, flaque, grogner, grommeler, siffler, claquer, vrombir... ?)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
